msgstr ""

msgid "The gRPC server"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The services are _served_ by a _server_.\n"
"Available services (_CDI beans_) are automatically registered and exposed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, the server is exposed on `localhost:9000`, and uses _plain-text_ "
"(so no TLS) when\n"
"running normally, and `localhost:9001` for tests."
msgstr ""

msgid "Run the application using: `mvn quarkus:dev`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Consuming a gRPC service"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this section, we are going to consume the service we expose.\n"
"To simplify, we are going to consume the service from the same application, "
"which in the real world, does not make sense."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open the existing `org.acme.ExampleResource` class, and edit the content to "
"become:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Inject the service and configure its name. The name is used in the "
"application configuration. If not specified then the field name is used "
"instead: `hello` in this particular case."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use the generated service interface based on Mutiny API."
msgstr ""

msgid "Invoke the service."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We need to configure the application to indicate where the `hello` service "
"is found.\n"
"In the `src/main/resources/application.properties` file, add the following "
"property:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`hello` is the name used in the `@GrpcClient` annotation."
msgstr ""

msgid "`host` configures the service host (here it's localhost)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Then, open http://localhost:8080/hello/quarkus in a browser, and you should "
"get `Hello quarkus`!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Packaging the application"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Like any other Quarkus applications, you can package it with: `mvn package`.\n"
"You can also package the application into a native executable with: `mvn "
"package -Pnative`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Generating Java files from proto with protobuf-maven-plugin"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Alternatively to using Quarkus code generation to generate stubs for `proto` "
"files, you can also use\n"
"`protobuf-maven-plugin`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To do it, first define the 2 following properties in the `<properties>` "
"section:"
msgstr ""

msgid "They configure the gRPC version and the `protoc` version."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Then, add to the `build` section the `os-maven-plugin` extension and the "
"`protobuf-maven-plugin` configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `protobuf-maven-plugin` that generates stub classes from your gRPC "
"service definition (`proto` files)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The class generation uses a tool named `protoc`, which is OS-specific.\n"
"That's why we use the `os-maven-plugin` to target the executable compatible "
"with the operating system."
msgstr ""

msgid "gRPC classes from dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When gRPC classes - the classes generated from `proto` files - are in a "
"dependency of the application, then the dependency needs a Jandex index.\n"
"The `jandex-maven-plugin` can be used to create a Jandex index. More "
"information on this topic can be found in the xref:cdi-reference."
"adoc#bean_discovery[Bean Discovery] section of the CDI guide."
msgstr ""
